    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21035" root="سهد" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُهُدٌ</span></b>  One <i>who sleeps little;</i> (S, A, L, K;) as
also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَهَّدٌ</span></b> : (A:) and some say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُهَدُ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمَرُ</span>;
but this is [of a measure used] only in proper
names: (Ham p. 39:) and an eye (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْنٌ</span>) <i>that
sleeps little.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] (tropical:)  <i>Vigilant; cautious;</i>
applied to a man; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَهَّدٌ</span></b> . (A, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
And <i>Little sleep.</i> (L.)

